WEBVTT

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.850
The prostitute who was the first victim

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:25.060
was last seen with a blond, fair-skinned
man who stood six feet tall...

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.940
...and was later found
barely recognisable.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.070
Her corpse had her throat slit, and her
internal organs had been removed.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.490
Then, a week later, another
prostitute was seen with a man

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:45.790
who had a swarthy complexion
and stood five and a half feet tall.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.420
Immediately afterward,
she was killed in an identical manner.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.510
Based on the eyewitness reports,

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.470
we surmised that one of
the two men is the killer,

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.350
and no sooner did we begin
our investigation...

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:06.020
...than a man calling himself "Jack the
Ripper" claimed credit for the crimes.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.230
Lestrade, did you...

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:10.820
...make this just for me?

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.450
Yes! I wanted it to be
an apt present for you.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.160
So allow me to ask you once again.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:21.910
I'd like you to help me catch this
criminal before another victim turns up.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.910
Please, Holmes!

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.170
No.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:50.020
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.780
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.910
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:00.950
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.370
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.750
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.130
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:17.720
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.300
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.430
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:29.060
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:33.190
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.280
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.610
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:44.080
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.960
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.750
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:02:58.800 --> 00:02:59.590
"The Phantom of Whitechapel Act 2"

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:04.100
"The Phantom of Whitechapel Act 2"
Young Will, you already have a guess as
to the identity of the culprit, don't you?

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.970
Yes. The culprit...

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:11.060
...is more than one person.
In fact, this is organised crime.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.440
What do you base that assessment on?

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.110
First, why would the killers
claim to be Jack the Ripper

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.240
and write to the newspapers?

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:26.490
Their objective is nothing else but to
proclaim their criminal acts far and wide,

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:31.710
and to whip up the fears
of the city's people.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.170
The fact that they adopted
the maestro's old nickname

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.800
is likely just an odd coincidence.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:41.180
Any name that would stoke fear
would have been sufficient.

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.350
Thus, it is presumable
that killing the prostitutes

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.020
was not their goal, but a means to an end.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:53.560
Which means that these serial killings
are all for dramatic effect,

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.650
meant to stoke the people's fears to
bring some other objective to pass.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.070
What other objective?

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:02.740
That would be...

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:06.070
...to incite conflict between the town's
Vigilance Committee and the Yard,

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:09.660
and once the two sides begin to clash...

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:13.710
...to set off a proletarian
revolution within Britain.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:20.050
Indeed. It would be difficult to consider

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:25.390
any one person being able to carry out
such a large undertaking on their own.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:30.180
The culprits fashioned this virtual devil
that they call "Jack the Ripper,"

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:34.100
setting the stage for the Vigilance
Committee to take up arms.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.100
If another murder occurs,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.400
a conflict between the Yard and the
Vigilance Committee will be unavoidable,

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.780
and will serve as the
trigger for an uprising.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.990
If this is true, then we have a problem.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:49.330
With multiple culprits, we'll need
to round them all up in one shot.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.250
Not to worry.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:54.960
We'll make this an experiment
to further the Moriarty Plan.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.160
Oh, it's just a cat.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:48.930
You expect us to let the Yard
handle this case?!

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.680
This is our town,
and we'll protect it ourselves!

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:03.110
What's that?!

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:20.460
It is I, Jack the Ripper, whose terror
can still even a crying child!

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:24.340
As I stand by and watch,
the strangest thing has been happening.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:29.760
Are you thinking of starting a war here
in Whitechapel, and leaving me out of it?

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.800
This works out just fine for me.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:35.470
Now I can keep on killing
as much as I like!

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:52.030
What's the matter?
Aren't you going to catch me?

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.170
After him!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.500
Make sure he doesn't escape!

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.000
--Sir!
--We're on him, too!

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.500
Yeah!

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:12.050
So that's it. By playing
the enemy for both sides,

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:16.310
the old man is unifying the Yard and the
Vigilance Committee, not dividing them.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:18.100
Yes.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:22.980
Fred, I want you to go procure three
autopsied bodies from the morgue.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.440
Very well. I will prepare some
stage blood, as well.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.110
Moran and Bonde, I need you to
pick up some weapons from Herder.

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.740
Who is Herder?

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:36.740
A friend of ours. Probably the biggest
weapon freak in all of London.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:40.910
Once Jack the Ripper shows up,
the criminals are sure to gather together

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:45.000
and plan out their next move.
That is when we'll hit them.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.170
But how will we pin down where they are?

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:53.640
We will consult the data from military
intelligence, with Albert's help.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:57.470
Maestro, I'll need you to buy
some time until I can confirm

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.730
that they have all assembled.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.690
I see, so this is a game of tag,
rather than hide-and-seek.

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:06.980
But can he keep running? Between
the Yard and the Vigilance Committee,

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:10.900
we're talking about no less than 300 men.
And if he can't kill anyone...

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.950
Killing is not allowed, of course, and I
would like you to avoid fighting back.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:18.740
That's a pretty tall order. I'm not sure
I could last for ten minutes.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:22.410
I could probably keep
it up for half an hour.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.120
Two hours...

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:28.800
No, please hold out for more
than one hour, at the least.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.670
There he is!

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.630
Hold it, you rotter!

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.100
Young Will, this is a positively
insane plan you've concocted.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.480
Take aim!

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.820
What's up with that coat? Is it armour?!

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:55.320
Hold it!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.830
It being so heavy is a bit of a drawback,
but this isn't so bad.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.910
The mission I've been assigned
is to keep running.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.500
To not kill anyone, and to keep
from being captured myself,

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:09.840
as I do nothing but buy time until
all our enemies are in one place.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.300
It's him! Aim for his head!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.180
Wh-What was that?!
My gun just suddenly went off!

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:21.140
Give me that! I'll do it!

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:31.780
It looks like our sniper is many
times better than yours.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.750
I'm impressed you can hit them
with the unaided eye at this range.

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:47.170
Do you expect me to use that
laughably huge scope?

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:50.460
More of them! One at 2 o'clock,
and another at 10 o'clock.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.590
Yeah, I see them.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:55.340
All clear.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:59.050
None of them appear to have the faintest
idea that they've been sniped.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.560
Sounds like it did well.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:05.520
It's an enhanced prototype,

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:09.190
so I ventured out into the field like
this, just in case something happened,

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:12.940
but it looks as though my services
will not be needed.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.360
No, Herder.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:18.070
The trajectory does tend to slice a bit,
but it's something that can be adjusted.

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.910
Oh, then it does need some fine-tuning.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:24.160
I must say, though,
this gun is amazingly silent.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.250
Of course it is.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:30.380
Please make sure to bring it back to me.
I can't collect any data if you break it.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.090
Yeah, I know.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.920
The old man must be
pretty worn out by now.

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.930
We have to back him up,
no matter what it takes.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.340
Okay!

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.550
Over here!

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:44.060
Hold it!

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:50.350
Twenty people in front of me
and a larger crowd behind. Do I...

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:56.990
...dash down the alleyway? What do I do?
Which way? Tell me what to do, Fred!

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.580
Go straight, you say?

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:05.660
Seize him!

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.000
I'll take you at your word, Fred!

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.470
Damn, he got us!

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.300
What a monster!

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:29.390
I see. If I had turned down that way,
they would have beaten me senseless.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:34.150
You saved me, Fred.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:39.280
Reporting in! He's supposed to be
coming down this road any time now!

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:45.740
Good. Get that thing ready!
We'll show that murderer what for!

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.540
It can't be! Is that...

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.330
...a Gatling gun?!

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.940
Fire!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.190
Keep firing!

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:20.360
Turn him into Swiss cheese!

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:27.160
It's no good. Even if I shoot it,
I won't be able to disable that thing.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:31.370
If I could get a bullet down that barrel,
I might get it to misfire,

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.960
but the angle is all wrong from up here.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.460
Come with me, Moran!

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:55.690
Your idea is unorthodox, just like you!

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.570
Bonde!

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:36.900
I don't know who instigated this,
but the tide has turned.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:38.150
Oi!

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.940
That fake showing up has turned
the whole plan upside down!

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:46.200
Yes, I was just finding myself
extremely troubled, as well.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:50.120
After taking on their
request as their agent

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:56.170
and using the power of the media to build
up this mythical "Jack the Ripper"...

00:13:56.170 --> 00:14:00.210
...he has turned everything against us,
and in one move, turned the conflict

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:03.510
between the Vigilance Committee
and the Yard on its ear.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:11.810
Master...

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:13.970
Fred, are you...?

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:18.440
If you go through that door,
you can get to a safe sewer line.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:19.980
I will take it from here.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:22.400
Yeah, you're on.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:26.320
He's here! This way!

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:29.160
--You monster!
--Hold it, Jack!

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.000
I'm getting old, all right.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.540
Still, I bought you an hour, William.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.260
Confound it, the plan is ruined!

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:51.300
The vigilantes and the Yard were just
moments away from going at each other.

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:52.640
Don't lose your head.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:55.890
Once we kill the next prostitute,
the situation will turn around again.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:15:00.650
Yeah. We'll send the powers that be
who plague this country straight to hell!

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:01.860
Hold up...

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.280
Kill the lights!

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:14.540
Hell... has been deserted.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.870
All of its devils...

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.210
...are right here.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:32.050
Who are you blokes?!

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:35.970
James Moriarty. Or rather...

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:39.980
...if I say the Lord of Crime,
does that make it simpler for you?

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.150
<i>You're </i>the Lord of Crime?

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:47.570
We are here to deliver your punishment.
For the Jack the Ripper incidents--

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.610
the serial killings of prostitutes.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.610
H-He knows what's really going on--

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.070
Wait.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:58.500
You are trying to plunge
the country into chaos--

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.920
which is to say, start a revolution,
yourselves, right?

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.880
Then we are both of the same mind.

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:08.050
We are on the verge of delivering
a stunning blow to the nation

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:10.760
over the insignificant lives
of a few prostitutes.

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.630
If we were to work together,

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:17.220
then could we not make our
sublime purpose a reality?

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:20.270
Are you saying that you think nothing

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:23.400
of unequivocally preying on the lives
of those weaker than yourselves

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.480
for your revolution?

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:28.860
Of course! The strong take from the weak.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:33.610
The law of the jungle is the providence
of the natural world, after all.

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:38.990
Heh, is that so? I am relieved
to hear you say that.

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.790
Then by your own reasoning...

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:48.670
...you will have no quarrel when we
unequivocally take your lives from you.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:50.090
Why, you...!

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.840
That's your response, is it?

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:54.680
Then kill them!

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.350
Eight of them. Got that, Louis?

00:16:57.350 --> 00:17:00.640
Yes, Brother. We kill them all.

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.310
You...!

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.320
Th-They're too much!

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.870
We'll be killed!

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.120
Go around to the back!
We'll get out on the boat!

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:22.330
Yeah!

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:32.710
What a pity. As long
as those chaps survive,

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:35.550
they can start everything over
as many times as it takes!

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:44.020
We had plenty of time whilst
the rest of you assembled.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:46.270
Y-You what?

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.650
Now...

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:56.200
...between the speed of
their heels and this fuse...

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:59.780
...which do you suppose is faster?

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:14.260
There's the way out!

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.140
We're going to get away--

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:29.190
Moran...

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:33.070
Yeah, that's the signal that the mission
is over. Let's get out of here.

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:40.780
All that remains are the bodies.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:42.950
You're sure you want to leave them here?

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.040
Yes.

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:49.460
The Yard will be along shortly.
Sooner or later, Holmes will arrive, too.

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:53.840
Knowing Holmes, he is certain to figure
out the full story behind this case.

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:56.970
I'd like to learn what his
reaction is when he does.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:19:00.890
You mean whether Holmes will
adopt the inconvenient truth,

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:04.560
or the more convenient lie,
is that what you mean?

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:06.180
That's right.

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:09.270
Is that...!?

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:13.570
If I recall, his name is
William James Moriarty.

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:18.240
Second son of the Moriarty family,
the young mathematics prodigy.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:23.160
I see. So that is the man
with whom I am competing.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:29.500
Then I must thoroughly investigate him
at once, and add him to the list.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:35.300
Yes, the list... kept by me,
Charles Augustus Milverton.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.600
Gruesome.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:49.310
It's largely difficult to determine the
cause of death due to the explosion,

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:52.600
but judging by these stab wounds,
I can say that this is the work of a pro.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.480
We concluded the same thing.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.950
Have you determined anything by
looking at the crime scene, Holmes?

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:02.780
Sherlock?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.620
Huh? Yeah.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:11.460
These are likely the victims
of Jack the Ripper, too.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.210
After stabbing them all to death,

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:16.590
he used the explosion as
a decoy to get away clean.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.010
That makes sense.

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:21.930
Then we will cordon off the area
and go after Jack the Ripper.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.260
Thank you, Holmes.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:31.350
Honestly... there is such a thing
as an inopportune truth.

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:34.520
Whilst keeping at bay the
worst-case scenario of a conflict

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:39.820
between the Yard and the Vigilance
Committee, the case itself was solved.

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:45.240
There's only one person who could
pull off that kind of sleight of hand.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:48.830
But he's almost playing Robin Hood!

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:53.420
What exactly are you thinking,
Lord of Crime?

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:57.090
So that was your choice after all, Holmes.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.840
Which means that the
administrators at the Yard

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:03.300
will not be content to allow Jack
to remain at large like this.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:07.180
The next move they
will consider will be...

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:24.700
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:32.910
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:43.510
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:46.890
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:50.890
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:54.270
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:21:54.270 --> 00:22:01.690
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:10.280
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:18.080
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:24.340
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:27.130
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:32.810
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:22:32.810 --> 00:22:39.480
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:49.160
W-William!

00:22:49.160 --> 00:22:49.990
What's the matter?

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.490
What <i>isn't </i>the matter?!
What's going on here?!

00:22:52.490 --> 00:22:56.410
Why are you so upset, Moran?

00:22:56.410 --> 00:22:59.920
Leave it to you, Maestro.
Very fashionable indeed.

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:04.130
Naturally. Right now,
<i>this </i>is my main line of work.

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:07.130
We wanted it to be a surprise
for you, Moran.

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:10.550
From now on, the maestro
will be serving as our butler.

00:23:10.550 --> 00:23:11.720
Huh?!

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:17.140
I could not bear to ask Louis to keep
house in <i>two </i>residences by himself.

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:21.480
This will make it easier for Louis
to take part in our plan.

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:24.940
Yes. Thank you so much
for your thoughtfulness.

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:26.110
Wha--?!

00:23:26.110 --> 00:23:28.490
I look forward to working alongside you.

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:32.490
What's the matter, Moran?
You look a little pale.

00:23:32.490 --> 00:23:36.160
Are you kidding me?!

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:50.630
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Riot in New Scotland Yard."
